On 19.03.2011 20:19, Peter J Ley wrote:
> 
> My question is, if I want to seriously start playing to ascend, should
> I concentrate on one role so I can get really good with it, or spread
> it around more to learn more general strategies?

Depends on whether your goal is to get an ascension fast, or whether
you want to learn more tactics and strategies and become able to use
a multitude of proficiencies in your games, thus increasing your
overall proficiency and reducing the risk to kill your characters.
Another approach is to play classes considered to be hard, but that
may be frustrating at first.

For a fast ascension experience try dwarven valkyries (fighters).
For a multitude of non-fighter proficiencies; healers and tourists,
rangers and rogues (ranged fighters), wizards.

> Also, is it really worth it to watch ttyrecs of ascensions? 

I'd suggest to watch also non-ascension games. You'll probably learn
from (observed and own) mistakes more than from pure ascension games.

